# A source of your choice may be an object an ability on the stack refers to "even if that object is no longer in the zone it
# used to be in" (CR 609.7a). Bot2 sacrifices its Fanatical Firebrand to have it deal 1 damage to Bot1; in response Bot1 casts
# Eye for an Eye and chooses the sacrificed Firebrand. The ability's damage is dealt by the Firebrand as it last existed - the
# chosen source - so Bot1 is still dealt it and Eye for an Eye deals 1 to that source's controller, Bot2. The effect is not
# ended because the object it was made about has left the battlefield.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl x2
Eye for an Eye
Island x25

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Fanatical Firebrand
Island x25

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Fanatical Firebrand.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Fanatical Firebrand.Activate(Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Eye for an Eye.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Fanatical Firebrand)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 19
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Graveyard = Fanatical Firebrand
